# Gensou Suikoden (SLPS-00097): 16-bit codes, low byte first (46 00 = あ). One table for the whole game.
# The code is the glyph's place in the game's 12x12 font, which stands whole in video memory during play.
# Read off that font glyph by glyph, then checked twice: against sentences in the game's own codes (the system
# text on the disc and the opening's dialogue in memory), which gave roughly two thirds of the 530 kanji a
# sentence, and glyph by glyph beside a reference 12-pixel font. The checks corrected four kanji (0x0116,
# 0x01AA, 0x023D, 0x025E). 0x0010 is the blank cell of the text grid. Not mapped: 0x0000-0x000F (window frame
# pieces), 0x0035-0x003B (cursor and wait marks), 0x00F2-0x00F7 (item icons). 0x01EA and 0x02B5 are both 退.
# Least certain: ＋ and － (0x00F0, 0x00F1), ” (0x00DD), 叉 (0x02CF).
